From d8388417f11ae5c8655d875b5ed3cc3f3427d081 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: snowf14k3 <60956553+snowf14k3@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 22:34:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: preserve the IRIS1 interrupt mask at boot

The SM8150 Android Q driver selects VPU5 and uses read-modify-write
in interrupt_init_vpu5(). It unmasks only the CPU and watchdog
interrupts while preserving every other wrapper interrupt mask bit.
Its documented reset mask is 0x1f6, resulting in 0x1e2 rather than the
VPU4 constant 0x8.

The fixed raphael-7.1 baseline has an IRIS1 VPU identifier but would
take the VPU4 constant-write path when an IRIS1 platform is added.
Add the dedicated branch using the existing legacy watchdog bit 4
and CPU bit 2 definitions. Do not use the IRIS2 watchdog bit or
register layout.

This is a preparatory change only. No SM8150 resource or device-tree
binding is added, and hardware decoding is not claimed. Other VPU
paths, PM, DMA, formats and encoder session code are unchanged.

Link: https://github.com/MiCode/Xiaomi_Kernel_OpenSource/blob/192eca8550f95c2eec58a474793d1d93fc1b3b67/drivers/media/platform/msm/vidc/venus_hfi.c#L4672-L4683
Signed-off-by: snowf14k3 <60956553+snowf14k3@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_venus.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_venus.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_venus.c
index bd82066bb..7c3440dd0 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_venus.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_venus.c
@@ -473,7 +473,11 @@ static int venus_boot_core(struct venus_hfi_device *hdev)
 	void __iomem *wrapper_base = hdev->core->wrapper_base;
 	int ret = 0;
 
-	if (IS_IRIS2(hdev->core) || IS_IRIS2_1(hdev->core)) {
+	if (IS_IRIS1(hdev->core)) {
+		mask_val = readl(wrapper_base + WRAPPER_INTR_MASK);
+		mask_val &= ~(WRAPPER_INTR_MASK_A2HWD_BASK |
+			      WRAPPER_INTR_MASK_A2HCPU_MASK);
+	} else if (IS_IRIS2(hdev->core) || IS_IRIS2_1(hdev->core)) {
 		mask_val = readl(wrapper_base + WRAPPER_INTR_MASK);
 		mask_val &= ~(WRAPPER_INTR_MASK_A2HWD_BASK_V6 |
 			      WRAPPER_INTR_MASK_A2HCPU_MASK);
-- 
